// What the Ash Remembers [B] (bible 4.3, 8.3): Aldermere asked the Unwriters to let it go. Wren arrives on its last
// day. Attend it to the end, or try to stop it and the Choir sings over the square (boss 6.6).
// Aldermere_2, the square. Mayor Hollin, a thrush, speaks for the village; Teodor stands at the edge.

title: Aldermere_Teodor
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.aldermere.attended")>>
    Teodor: The square is paper now. They are in the Blank, cartographer. They asked for that. They are well. #still #line:03bf87a
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("verdance.aldermere.stopped")>>
    Hollin: You are the one who stopped it. Thank you, I suppose. We are still here. We are still here. #still #line:085ae22
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Hollin: Welcome to Aldermere. There is bread. There is always bread on the last day. #line:067ff9b
Hollin: We voted. Every hand. The Guild wanted four hundred crowns a street, and then we would be the same forever. #line:0dc835b
Hollin: We would rather be remembered than kept. The brothers were kind enough to ask us twice. #line:0af2746
Teodor: Three times. I asked three times. I made sure. #line:01bb513
-> Then I'll stay to the end. #line:0927bd2
    <<jump Aldermere_Attend>>
-> I won't let you fade. #line:0bdd5a3
    <<jump Aldermere_Stop>>
-> Who will remember you? #line:03aa299
    Hollin: You will. That is why we are glad you came. A visitor is the best kind of memory. #line:01796f6
    <<jump Aldermere_Attend>>
===

title: Aldermere_Attend
---
Hollin: Stay by the bread. The bells start at dusk. It does not hurt. Brother Teodor has done this before. #line:098c7b0
Teodor: The kindest thing you will see, cartographer. I am glad it is you watching. #line:027960b
Hollin: When you pass again, do not look for us. Look for the ash field. We will be in it. #line:095ba84
<<release Verdance_Aldermere_1>>
<<release Verdance_Aldermere_2>>
<<release Verdance_Aldermere_3>>
<<flag verdance.aldermere.attended 1>>
<<flag verdance.aldermere.decided 1>>
===

title: Aldermere_Stop
---
Teodor: Ah. May I say a thing you will not like? They did not ask you. #line:056adf3
Hollin: Please. Put the quill down. We voted. #line:07e3080
-> Put the bells down, then. #line:086ca69
    Teodor: The Choir will not. They sing what was asked of them. I will neither stop them nor help them. #line:0aedf36
-> ... #line:035eb61
    Teodor: Then you must answer the Choir. I am sorry. It is the one thing I am sorry for today. #line:070896b
<<flag verdance.aldermere.stopped 1>>
<<flag verdance.aldermere.decided 2>>
===
